{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0008961","label":"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4A","definition":"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4A (CMT4A) is a subtype of Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4 characterized by early-onset (infancy to early childhood) of severe, rapidly progressing demyelinating, axonal, or intermediate sensorimotor neuropathy usually affecting first, and more severely, the distal lower extremities and later the proximal muscles and upper extremities. Nerve conduction velocities range from very slow to normal. Apart from the typical CMT phenotype (distal muscle weakness and atrophy, sensory loss, frequent pes cavus foot deformity), patients commonly present delayed motor development, vocal cord paresis, mild sensory loss, abolished deep tendon reflexes, and skeletal deformities.","synonyms":["CMT4A","Charcot Marie Tooth disease type 4A","Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4 caused by mutation in GDAP1","Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease, type 4A","GDAP1 Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4"],"xrefs":["DOID:0110185","GARD:0001252","MEDGEN:347821","MESH:C535419","OMIM:214400","Orphanet:99948","SCTID:715796006","UMLS:C1859198","icd11.foundation:1476665103"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":54,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_e01490cdd0ed","source":"MONDO:0008961","target":"GDAP1","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:99948","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/99948","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — ganglioside induced differentiation associated protein 1"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:214400","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://omim.org/entry/214400","snippet":"GDAP1 is annotated as disease gene of OMIM:214400 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, OMIM-derived)"}],"contradict